<description>
**Problem:** Test helpers that attach active-tip templates to arbitrary parents retain the template's subsidy.
Existing reorg tests can underpay without failing, while a fork crossing a halving can overpay and fail with `bad-cb-amount`.
Coinbase input scripts containing only the height also fail with `bad-cb-length` at heights 1 through 16.

**Fix:** Share parent-dependent reconstruction between `BuildChain()` and `MinerTestingSetup::Block()`, deriving difficulty and coinbase fields from the actual parent.
Pad rebuilt coinbase input scripts and require coinbase-only templates so replacing the reward with the subsidy cannot discard transaction fees.
</description>

<commits>
9fdac77721 test: characterize fork coinbase fields

Record the subsidy and input-script length of a chain built from genesis through the first halving.
The active-tip template reward is retained at the halving, and the unpadded low-height coinbases prevent the fork from connecting.

Co-authored-by: JP <jeanpablo.jp@hotmail.com>

7e784f41a0 refactor: extract fork block reconstruction

Move the existing parent-dependent field rewrites out of `BuildChain()` without changing the generated fields.
A direct helper test records the copied target using a synthetic parent with a different target on either side of regtest's min-difficulty delay.

Co-authored-by: JP <jeanpablo.jp@hotmail.com>

d9f4511475 test: derive fork difficulty from parent

Recalculate `nBits` from the actual parent and child timestamp instead of retaining the active-tip template's target.
Existing chain-building callers use regtest's minimum difficulty, so their generated targets are unchanged.

7bb37739db test: derive fork subsidy from parent

Derive the coinbase subsidy from the actual parent height and share the reconstruction with `MinerTestingSetup::Block()`.
Existing reorg tests cross halvings and underpay some coinbases, which remains valid and does not fail the tests. A fork extending across a halving can instead overpay and fail with `bad-cb-amount`.

Require coinbase-only templates so replacing the reward cannot discard transaction fees.

27240dce14 test: pad fork coinbase input scripts

Append a dummy `OP_0` to rebuilt coinbase input scripts so heights 1 through 16 meet the minimum length.
The fork from genesis can then connect through the first halving. Remove the validation helper's duplicate padding.
</commits>

